{"title":"1996 OIM Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have a board of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df60367ab3d79da3a763ba1b74c310ca73f9c489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2-k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df60367ab3d79da3a763ba1b74c310ca73f9c489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2-k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> columns, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/771abfacf3f0d119f01b75de06bc9b5f9b1badb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime number. For each prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, provide a method for distributing numbers 0 and 1, a number in each square of the board, so that in each row there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> numbers 0 and also there are no rectangles with parallel sides on the sides of the board with numbers 0 in its four vertices.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 46/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1042/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.607      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    6.607      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26103:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190001 and revision id 207082. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}